   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.1. To facilitate the use of technology in customer due diligence processes of financial institutions, the Financial Intelligence Unit undertook a diagnostic report to examine the suitability of the existing legal and regulatory framework, as the basis for further reforms, for use of technology.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.2. To support the online registration of identities from remote locations, the Department of Civil Registration and Identity Management established an updated identity database and confirm accuracy, completeness, and compliance with established standards.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.3. To facilitate a conducive environment for data-sharing between the private and public sectors, the government issued a policy to ensure data privacy and security, which will comply with global standards</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.4. To support the international exchange of information on request, the Minister of Finance and Economic Management approved and gazetted regulations under the Tax Administration Act to establish a framework for the exchange of information on beneficial owners of legal entities with competent authorities internationally</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.1. To facilitate trade and growth in business opportunities, the Ministry of Trade and Commerce: (i) established a platform for businesses&#x2019; online submission and payments for import and export certificates, licenses, and permits, and (ii) issues certificates of origin online</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.2. To facilitate the development of commerce and industry, the Ministry for Trade, and Commerce approved an e-commerce strategy with women&#x2019;s empowerment included in the strategic framework.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">4.1. To manage disaster risks and support sustainable financing, the Council of Ministers approved: (i) The National Disaster Risk Finance Policy 2024-2029 that lays the policy framework to enhance the financial protection of Vanuatu against disasters; and (ii) a framework for the issuance of sustainable bonds, which outlines how bonds could finance projects that deliver environmental and social benefits, including to address climate change, in Vanuatu.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Grant 1001: 0% of contracts awarded and 100% disbursed as of 01 Feb 2025</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
